BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ukulele for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T150000
UID:6aaac9ba101eb7003f309413@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to learn an instrument? Try learning to play with ukulele
 . We provide the ukulele\, and you can come with an open mind. Ukulele for
  Beginners is a series of 4 classes. Attendees should attend all four clas
 ses\, (November 4\, 11\, 18\, 25) which will cover fundamentals of ukulele
  playing: the parts of a ukulele\, tuning\, strumming patterns\, and some 
 basic chords.\nPlease register\, if you need to borrow a ukulele for this 
 session.\nIf you have your own instrument\, you may drop-in\, no registrat
 ion needed.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaac9ba101eb7003f309413
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python IV
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T200000
UID:6a97328c4cb69d003e250170@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Python is an open source programming language that is used for
  creating web applications\, web content\, mathematics and system scriptin
 g. In this follow up course we will take our understanding of data structu
 res to the next level as well as looking into the next stages of error han
 dling (including making some custom error messages) and extending our know
 ledge of input/output to more than just the terminal.\nThis class is for b
 eginners but assumes you have a basic understanding of Python or have atte
 nded Coding with Python I\, II\, and III.\nRegistration will start 2 weeks
  before this class\n. This program is hosted on Zoom. The Zoom informatio
 n and link will be shared over email.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-598
 1\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a97328c4cb69d003e250170
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DJ At Any Age: Memories in the Mix
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T200000
UID:6aa062565ecd9e1b553241c7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bring out your inner DJ in this intergenerational program for 
 seniors and adults. Learn basic djing skills and connect with others over 
 a shared love of music. Artist and educator Deejay Vee from At Any Age wil
 l teach you how to use a dj controller and software in a fun and relaxed a
 tmosphere. Working individually or in pairs\, you'll create and exchange p
 laylists of songs that represent meaningful moments in your life.\nNo prio
 r experience needed.\nThis 5-week program series takes place every Thursda
 y from November 12th – December 10th.\nWeeks 1 – 4: Learn DJing skills
 .\nWeek 5: Showcase! Perform your new skills for the group and your friend
 s and family. Refreshments will be provided. Ingredient list will be ava
 ilable at the program.\nInformation Collection Notice\n: The personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, 1st Floor\, Children's Programming Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa062565ecd9e1b553241c7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
