BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for a Just World: Power\, Liberation\, and the People Left Behi
 nd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T120000
UID:6aa45d8186d8450031156b48@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How is artificial intelligence reshaping healthcare\, work\, a
 nd state surveillance? And what can we do about it?  In this interactive p
 anel discussion\, we present three real-world case studies. With each case
  study\, we ask: how are communities being affected\, and how are they res
 isting? First\, we consider promises being made to the sickle cell communi
 ty about the role of AI in diagnosis and cure. Second\, we consider the ro
 le of AI in delivery worker exploitation.  Digital platform workers are al
 ready living the future that concerns so many of us. Third\, we consider h
 ow AI is reshaping warfare and state surveillance. After each case study\,
  we will pose small-group questions for the audience to discuss.\nAbout ou
 r speakers: Rachel da Silveira Gorman (Professor\, Graduate Program Dire
 ctor\, Critical Disability Studies)\, Vanessa Ferguson (PhD Candidate\, 
 School of Health Policy & Management at York University)\, Emmett Lockwoo
 d (PhD Student in Critical Disability Studies at York University)\, and H
 abiba Rahman (PhD candidate in Critical Disability Studies at York Univers
 ity)\n***\nAbout this event\nDigital Expo 2026 is a dynamic day of learnin
 g\, exploration\, and connection focused on shaping a responsible AI futur
 e for everyone.\nFeaturing inspiring speakers and interactive exhibits\, a
 s well as hands-on workshops for adults\, kids and teens\, the event explo
 res how emerging technologies are transforming our lives\, communities and
  civic institutions.\nTogether\, we'll examine the opportunities and chall
 enges of AI to foster a more informed\, inclusive and empowered digital so
 ciety that protects Canadians and safeguards democracy.\nCheck out tpl.ca/
 digitalexpo for more information about the Expo and the workshops.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa45d8186d8450031156b48
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
