SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Make Your Own Interactive Story with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T200000
UID:6a9b51b13b6c71003e5de7bf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could write a story where the reader chooses what 
 happens\, like a branching adventure\, a mystery\, or a game\, and have AI
  build it with you?\nIn this class\, you'll learn "vibe-coding": using an 
 AI coding assistant to build your own interactive story or simple game. Yo
 u'll design the branches\, describe the rules in plain language\, test for
  the tricky edge cases (what if the player picks the weird option?)\, and 
 end up with a single file you can share with anyone. Just a story you want
  to tell. This is the playful sibling of the practical vibe-coding worksho
 p.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guar
 anteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, rem
 aining seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capa
 city is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on program
 \, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Progr
 am\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed bel
 ow) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for th
 is program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidan
 ce throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe enc
 ourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attendin
 g this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy po
 licy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy polic
 y\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is coll
 ected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, secti
 ons 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event
