BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Get Things Done with AI: Build Your Own Productivity System
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T180000
UID:6a9b51af3b6c71003e5de7bd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if your to-do list could check in on you\, notice what's 
 been stuck for weeks\, and offer to help instead of just sitting there?\nI
 n this class\, you'll explore a personal productivity system built around 
 an AI agent and a weekly-review practice. See how the agent loads goals\, 
 counts what actually got done\, flags the items that keep slipping\, and d
 rafts next week's plan. It can support without cheerleading\, asking "Why 
 has this been stuck for three weeks? Here are your options." You'll try it
  yourself with a practice set of goals\, and leave with the plain-text tem
 plates and a clearer map of how an AI might support you\, ready to build y
 our own system at home.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet 
 skills. Computers are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistra
 tion is required and will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your 
 spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\n
 After this time\, remaining seats will be filled on a first come\, first s
 erve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from 
 this hands-on program\, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Too
 ls Used in This Program\nThis program includes activities that use agentic
  AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create yo
 ur own account for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow th
 e Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practices
  on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of each t
 ool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the to
 ol\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nRevie
 w privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview p
 rivacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy
  policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this 
 form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries
  Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be us
 ed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions
  about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerl
 ine staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toro
 nto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51af3b6c71003e5de7bd
