DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T160000
UID:6a986aa62dac6e00372391bb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Opening up a business brings new opportunities\, but it also b
 rings challenges.  Incorporation Basics will cover the essential ins and o
 uts of starting a business. Learn the differences between a corporation an
 d other types of businesses\, the important terminology for corporations\,
  how to properly register and set up a corporation\, and the basics of run
 ning a corporation. The pros and cons of setting up a corporation will als
 o be discussed.\nThe presenter\, Samuel Michaels\, is the founding lawyer 
 of SM Legal. Samuel practices primarily in corporate law and has a strong 
 background in both corporate law and employment law. Samuel is also a pass
 ionate advocate for access to justice and legal education.\nDrop in. No re
 gistration required.\nThis program is part of Small Business Month.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First Floor Program Room (CPR)
