UID:6a97641157c264087ad58db5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Junction Triangle Library and its neighbourhood is home to
  a variety of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to expl
 ore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recogniz
 e different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological impo
 rtance.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver. Regi
 stration is required.\nThe tour will start and end at the Junction Triangl
 e Library and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff.
  There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and 
 prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\,
  sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or 
 shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, registrants will be noti
 fied of an alternative date.
LOCATION:Junction Triangle
