BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Run Your One-Person Business with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T180000
UID:6a9b51bb1c197d11325d7089@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When you're the whole company\, the admin never ends: emails\,
  scheduling\, proposals\, follow-ups. What if you could design a system to
  handle the busywork?\nIn this class\, you'll learn to design an administr
 ative system for a one-person business with AI as your assistant: intake p
 ipelines\, email drafting\, client communication\, and scheduling. Learn t
 o map work into four piles: what's rules-based\, what AI drafts\, what nee
 ds your judgment\, and what should never be automated. You'll build reusab
 le templates and leave with a clearer plan for how AI could help your busi
 ness.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers
  are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required a
 nd will start November 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be 
 guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\,
  remaining seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until 
 capacity is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on pro
 gram\, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This P
 rogram\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed
  below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account fo
 r this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s gu
 idance throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe
  encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to atte
 nding this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privac
 y policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\
 nGoogle Antigravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoo
 gle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51bb1c197d11325d7089
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Python Essentials 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T180000
UID:6ab182a5129d8e0031f40d44@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn Python and build your programming skills in a supportive
  group. This learning circle will meet on Monday evenings from November 2
  to December 7\, 4-6pm. Learning circles are study groups guided by staff
  for people who want to take a free online course together in a welcoming 
 space. Learners meet weekly and work together through the course materials
 . Participants are expected to commit to the duration of the course and at
 tend all learning circle sessions.\nUsed by startups and tech giants like 
 Google\, Facebook\, Netflix\, and more\, Python offers you endless possibi
 lities for creating small and large-scale software projects. User-friendly
  with easy-to-read code\, Python is a great first programming language to 
 learn and requires no prior programming knowledge. Python skills open you 
 up to careers in almost any industry and are required if you want to conti
 nue to more advanced\, higher paying software development and engineering 
 roles such as software engineer\, systems administrator\, and security eng
 ineer.\nPython Essentials 1\nIn this course\, you will learn in-demand ski
 lls such as how to design\, develop\, and improve computer programs\, meth
 ods for analyzing problems using programming\, programming best practices\
 , and more. The course also prepares you for the PCEP – Certified Entry-
 Level Python Programmer certification (Exam PCEP-30-0x).\nFor more informa
 tion about the Python learning circle\, please contact\nnetworkingacademy@
 tpl.ca\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Brookbanks\, Lower Level Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab182a5129d8e0031f40d44
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
