BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Who Should Own AI? Building Public AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T160000
UID:6a9b51abaafa61002961b2a3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:If AI becomes as important as roads\, electricity\, or librari
 es\, who should own it? Who decides what it's used for? Who gets access an
 d to say no?\nThis panel discussion will include speakers building public-
 interest AI\, working in civic tech\, and organizing communities affected 
 by AI decisions. We'll explore what's already being built\, from open mode
 ls and public compute to community-owned data\, and what's being privatize
 d. You'll get to draft your own "public AI requirements" and see what othe
 rs think should be guaranteed to everyone. The future of AI is being decid
 ed now\; this is a chance to have a say in it.\nFeaturing:\nAlex Olson\n\,
  Director of University of Toronto’s Centre for Analytics & AI Engineeri
 ng\nKhasir Hean\n\, Founder of Technologists for Democracy\, Machine Learn
 ing engineer\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 2026 at 
 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the s
 tart of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on 
 a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nInformation C
 ollection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by t
 he Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\
 , 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progr
 am registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library
  handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerli
 ne@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51abaafa61002961b2a3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
