BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Introduction to Data Visualization and Storytelling
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T193000
UID:6a96f2bd5e6fc10d0550c5d0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Participate in an in-person program to learn data visualizati
 on\, storytelling\, and data literacy\, equipping participants with essent
 ial skills to transform data into compelling visual narratives. You will l
 earn about the most popular data visualization types\, best practices in d
 ata preparation\, and techniques for selecting effective charts. Through h
 ands-on exercises\, you will practice creating clear\, impactful visualiza
 tions that communicate data insights effectively. This course is ideal for
  those who want to enhance their data storytelling skills and build a stro
 ng foundation in data visualization.\nPrerequisites: Excel Basics Part 1 o
 r equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nThi
 s program takes place during Digital Inclusion Week 2026.
LOCATION:McGregor Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a96f2bd5e6fc10d0550c5d0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bring Your Problem: Can AI Help?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T160000
UID:6a9b4df62dac6e003724371a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a recurring problem you think AI might help with? 
 A thing you keep doing by hand that feels like it should be easier? Bring 
 it. If you don't have one\, come help your neighbours with theirs.\nIn thi
 s interactive class\, you'll learn a simple seven-step way to think about 
 problems: what's annoying you\, what you've tried\, what AI could actually
  do\, and where it would fail. We'll gather real problems from the room\, 
 sort them into groups\, and map out what's worth solving with AI\, and wha
 t's better solved without it. We'll also talk honestly about what an AI fi
 x costs: your money\, your time\, and sometimes your private information. 
 The problems AI could help with most are often the most personal\, and the
  most personal ones are worth the most care.\nThis program takes place dur
 ing\nDigital Inclusion Week 2026\n.\nRegistration is required and will sta
 rt September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed 
 after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining 
 seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is
  reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on thi
 s form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librari
 es Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be 
 used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questio
 ns about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answe
 rline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4df62dac6e003724371a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
