 oring the skills that help people participate in civic life\, build unders
 tanding and work together.\nIn this session\, we’ll exercise our\nDisagr
 eement\nmuscles. In a democracy\, disagreement is natural\, but it can fee
 l uncomfortable. If you can stay with disagreement\, you gain knowledge an
 d respect.\nThis program is for\nadults. Drop ins are welcome.\nThis progr
 am is offered in partnership with Democracy Fitness Global and MASS LBP.\n
 Generously supported by McConnell Foundation.\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa94bb53dd190003e720dd9
