BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Peek Inside an AI Assistant: How It Thinks and Works
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T200000
UID:6a9b4dfc3b6c71003e5de6c9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You've asked an AI chatbot questions. But there's another kind
  of AI that doesn't just answer: it acts.\nIn this demo-driven talk\, we'l
 l look deeply at always-on personal AI assistants. The assistant can read 
 your files\, use your apps\, and remember what you've told it\, growing mo
 re useful over time. The same powers that let it help you can hurt you if 
 something goes wrong. We'll also open up what happens inside: the hidden i
 nstructions\, the tools it uses\, what it remembers and forgets.\nThen we'
 ll look at the AI assistant that helped develop this workshop\, and how we
  shaped our workflow together\, and why.\nThis program takes place during\
 nDigital Inclusion Week 2026\n.\nRegistration is required and will start S
 eptember 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed afte
 r 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seat
 s will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is rea
 ched.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4dfc3b6c71003e5de6c9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
