SUMMARY:AI for Job Hunting: Build Your Own System
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T200000
UID:6a9b51a9aafa61002961b2a1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Job hunting is a job in itself: applications\, deadlines\, int
 erviews\, follow-ups. What if you could build your own AI-powered system t
 o help you manage it?\nIn this hands-on class\, you'll explore a job-hunti
 ng dashboard built with AI: how it tracks applications\, sets automatic al
 erts for postings that match you\, and practices interviews with you throu
 gh role-play. You'll leave with the templates to build your own. We'll als
 o talk about how employers screen applications\, and how it can make thing
 s unfair. Come explore a tool that works for you\, not the other way aroun
 d.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guar
 anteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, rem
 aining seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capa
 city is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on program
 \, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Progr
 am\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed bel
 ow) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for th
 is program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidan
 ce throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe enc
 ourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attendin
 g this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy po
 licy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoo
 gle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle
  AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation 
