BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for Small Business and Entrepreneurs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T200000
UID:6a9b51b8aafa61002961b2a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You've got the business idea. Now come the thousand questions:
  who's my customer\, what's the market\, how do I pitch this?\nIn this cla
 ss\, you'll use AI as a research and planning partner for small business. 
 We'll practice together on a sample business\, turning rough ideas into bu
 siness plans\, digging into markets\, drafting customer-discovery question
 s\, and building useful low-maintenance automation. The most valuable thin
 g you'll get is usually a better question to be tested in the real world. 
 Whether you're starting or growing\, you'll leave with an experiment you c
 an run on your own business this week.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboardin
 g and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding experience requ
 ired.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 P
 M.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of
  the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on a first
  come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf you wish to save 
 your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your own USB stick.\nA
 bout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activities t
 hat use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not ne
 ed to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are encourag
 ed to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which include
  best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy state
 ments of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn mo
 re about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about 
 the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the
  tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\
 nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal infor
 mation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the P
 ublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information 
 will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalua
 tion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dire
 cted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yong
 e Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51b8aafa61002961b2a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python V
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T200000
UID:6a97332669166f088b9690d2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Python is an open source programming language that is used for
  creating web applications\, web content\, mathematics and system scriptin
 g. In this follow up course we will take a break from the logical side of 
 back-end development and get our feet wet with a little bit of front-end c
 oding\; we'll make a user interface! Using tkinter\, a popular module for 
 creating user-facing layouts\, we will design and implement a simple but e
 ffective UI for our Python code. This will allow us to run our programs us
 ing another platform other than Terminal.\nThis class is for beginners but
  assumes you have a basic understanding of Python or have attended Coding 
 with Python I\, II\, III\, and IV.\nRegistration will start 2 weeks before
  this class\n. This program is hosted on Zoom. The Zoom information and l
 ink will be shared over email.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe person
 al information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library und
 er the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The info
 rmation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery an
 d evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can
  be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789
  Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a97332669166f088b9690d2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
