BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Democracy Fitness: A Workout for Meaningful Dialogue using your Op
 inion Muscle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T104500
UID:6a904c9f36204e08fbb78f91@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Developed in Denmark\, and now offered around the world\, this
  fun\, active 45-minute training focuses on building the essential
  skills of everyday democracy.\nLearn to build consciousness and self-awar
 eness around your own perspectives while engaging in dialogue with others 
 by using your opinion muscle. Through a series of short\, interactive exer
 cises\, you'll explore where your opinions fall on a variety of topics. Gu
 ided discussions with others who think similarly and differently from you 
 will help you deepen your understanding of diverse viewpoints and strength
 en your ability to engage in constructive dialogue across differences.\n**
 *\nAbout this event\nDigital Expo 2026 is a dynamic day of learning\, expl
 oration and connection focused on shaping a responsible AI future for ever
 yone.\nFeaturing inspiring speakers and interactive exhibits\, as well as 
 hands-on workshops for adults\, kids and teens\, the event explores how em
 erging technologies are transforming our lives\, communities and civic ins
 titutions.\nTogether\, we'll examine the opportunities and challenges of A
 I to foster a more informed\, inclusive and empowered digital society that
  protects Canadians and safeguards democracy.\nCheck out tpl.ca/digitalexp
 o for more information about the Expo and the workshops.\n***\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by
  the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a
 )\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pro
 gram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libra
 ry handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswer
 line@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\n***
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904c9f36204e08fbb78f91
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
