BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for Us: Shaping AI in Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T160000
UID:6a9b51beaafa61002961b2a7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto is one of the biggest AI cities in the world. But what
  do the people here actually think about it and how do we want to shape it
 s development and use?\nA panel of experts\, who know AI from very differe
 nt angles\, united for an open conversation about what AI is doing to this
  city\, and what we want it to do instead. We'll talk about:\nThe human be
 ings behind the machines: what drives the people who build AI\, and what w
 orries them.\nWork\, money\, and meaning: what happens to jobs\, creativit
 y\, and value when AI lands here.\nWho gets to shape it and who's left out
  (both are our neighbours).\nThe stories we tell: how art\, media\, news\,
  and everyday talk shape what we expect\, fear\, and hope for.\nNo pitches
 \, no boosterism. Just an honest conversation about the ideas and stories 
 shaping AI in this city\, and what we want it to become.\nFeaturing:\nJerr
 old McGrath\n\, Cultural Programmer and Theorist\, In the Meantime\nJoseph
  Wilson\n\, Anthropologist & Author of Humans of AI: Understanding the Hum
 ans Behind the Machines\nOwais Lightwala\n\, Assistant Professor\, Perform
 ance at The Creative School at Toronto Metropolitan University\, Director\
 ,\nChrysalis\nRegistration is required and will start November 9\, 2026 at
  12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the 
 start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on
  a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51beaafa61002961b2a7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI Everywhere\, All At Once
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T200000
UID:6a9b4de23b6c71003e5de6c5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI is suddenly everywhere\, in ads\, on your phone\, your news
  feed\, all your software\, even your search bar. Who decides what gets ma
 de with AI? What does it cost? And what does it feel like? What happens wh
 en these tools start to feel less like tools and more like collaborators?\
 nIn this kickoff event for our Innovator in Residence (Applied AI Developm
 ent) program\, join Ryan Kelln for an illustrated talk with live demos. Le
 t's think together deeply about the impact\, costs and opportunities prese
 nted when trillions of dollars are spent researching and developing digita
 l intelligence. We'll talk candidly about the people who make it\, why the
 y make it\, and how it shifts power. Then we'll look at what your library 
 can offer that the AI companies can't\, and how to get the most out of the
  12 week residency program ahead.\nRegistration is required and will start
  September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed af
 ter 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining se
 ats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is r
 eached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this 
 form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries
  Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be us
 ed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions
  about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerl
 ine staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toro
 nto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4de23b6c71003e5de6c5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
