BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI Dialogues: On Creative Industries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T200000
UID:6aa17079ac72f22c5568d5a8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The creative industries are being disrupted at a scale and spe
 ed unlike anything they've encountered before. Artificial intelligence can
  now generate images\, write scripts\, compose music\, and simulate voices
 . What's at stake goes far beyond technology. It cuts to the heart of auth
 orship\, labour\, ownership\, and the value we place on human expression.\
 nIn this program\, two voices at the intersection of AI and the creative i
 ndustry join us for a discussion about what this moment makes possible and
  the challenges and risks it presents.\nOur speakers:\nAna Serrano is Pres
 ident and Vice-Chancellor of OCAD University\, co-founder of DemocracyXCha
 nge\, and an award-winning leader in digital media and cultural innovation
 . She previously founded the CFC Media Lab and IDEABOOST at the Canadian F
 ilm Centre and has helped shape national conversations on democracy\, tech
 nology\, and culture.\nRyan Patterson is the creative director at Queen On
 e Studios\, an AI-native studio working in film/tv\, ads and education. Wi
 th over a decade of video production experience in advertising and communi
 cations\, he has been featured in Variety and Deadline\, spoken at the Tor
 onto International Film Festival and Adobe MAX\, and was named a Top 100 A
 I Creative on LinkedIn.\nModerated by author\, scholar and researcher Paol
 o Granata (University of Toronto)\, these two leading voices bring the ful
 l tension of this moment into focus\, not to resolve it\, but to help us t
 hink more clearly and critically about it. After their dialogue\, the conv
 ersation moves into the room. You'll be invited to discuss in small groups
 \, then join an open exchange with both speakers. No conclusion is require
 d.\nThis AI Dialogues program is presented in collaboration with the Provo
 cation Ideas Festival.\n*********\nAbout the AI Dialogues\nArtificial inte
 lligence is reshaping nearly every dimension of human life\, how we work\,
  how we govern\, how we heal\, how we connect. And yet\, for all its momen
 tum\, the conversation around AI is fragmented: hype on one side\, fear on
  the other\, and very little space in between for genuine\, grounded excha
 nge. The AI Dialogues is a series that creates that space.\nEach program b
 rings together two voices - experts\, practitioners\, and thinkers who hav
 e earned their perspectives through experience - to explore a single topic
  through the lens of AI's promise and its challenges. Then opens the floor
 \, inviting audiences into small group discussion before bringing every vo
 ice into a shared dialogue.\nThe goal is not consensus. It is clarity - th
 e kind that only comes from sitting with complexity\, listening across dis
 agreement\, challenging our assumptions\, and resisting the urge to resolv
 e what isn't yet resolved.\nAI will shape the future. How we think and tal
 k about it will shape it even more.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Concourse Event Space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa17079ac72f22c5568d5a8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
