SUMMARY:Democracy Fitness: Empathy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T153000
UID:6ab29ec6ca248a0029179219@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active parti
 cipant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive\n30-minute\nsession
 .\nDemocracy Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exp
 loring the skills that help people participate in civic life\, build conne
 ction\, and work better together.\nIn this session\, we’ll exercise our\
 nEmpathy Muscle:\nIn a democracy\, we have different perspectives. If we w
 ant to understand others and be understood\, we must put ourselves in each
  other's shoes.\nRegistration Recommended. Drop-ins welcome.\nAdults only.
 \nThis program is offered in partnership with Democracy Fitness Global and
  MASS LBP.\nGenerously supported by McConnell Foundation.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab29ec6ca248a0029179219
