BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Gravity Grand Prix
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T190000
UID:6a79f5b6cca66c2f00a98e97@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Gravity Grand Prix:\n3D Printed Car Competition\nGet ready
  to design\, build\, and race!\nThis high-speed engineering challenge invi
 tes\nyoung adults (competing in teams of 2)\nto design the ultimate gravit
 y-powered race car. Using professional 3D modeling software and cutting-ed
 ge 3D printing technology\, your team will compete to see who can conquer 
 the downhill track the fastest. The core of this challenge is physics:\nma
 ximizing kinetic energy while minimizing friction\n. How will you transfor
 m potential energy into pure speed?🛠️ The Challenge Rules\nThe Softwa
 re:\nAll cars must be fully designed from scratch using\nOnShape\n. A brie
 f Introduction to the software will be provided.\nThe Material Limit:\nTo 
 keep the playing field level\, your final race car is strictly limited to 
 a maximum of\n30 grams of 3D printed filament\nand\n2 tooth picks.\nFree P
 rototyping:\nFailure is part of engineering! Teams are encouraged to print
 \, test\, and redesign.\nPrototype prints are completely free\nthroughout 
 the design phase.\nThe Track:\nA straight\, downhill gravity track built f
 or maximum acceleration.\n📅 Timeline & Important Dates\nDesign & Protot
 yping Week:\nNov 4 to Nov 11— Access the DIH\, collaborate with your pa
 rtner\, and test your prototypes.\nRace Day:\nNov 11\n(Exactly one week af
 ter design week)\n— Family and friends are welcome to watch the final sh
 owdown!\n💡 Key Engineering Focus Areas to take home the trophy\, your t
 eam will need to think critically about:\nAerodynamics & Friction:\nHow wi
 ll you reduce air resistance and wheel friction to keep your car gliding?\
 nWeight Distribution:\nHow can you strategically place your 30-gram limit 
 to maximize downward momentum?
LOCATION:Malvern\, Inside the Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a79f5b6cca66c2f00a98e97
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
