DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T143000
UID:6ab543d76074830038293bea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:OCTOBER IS ISLAMIC HERITAGE MONTH\nDive into the art of Arabic
  calligraphy in this 90-minute workshop. Learn the history and basics of A
 rabic script\, including how to hold the pen\, scaling\, and beginner exer
 cises to build precision. Explore Creative Dimensions like letter variatio
 ns\, stroke adjustments\, and integration through live demonstrations. Per
 fect for beginners\, this session blends tradition with creativity\, givin
 g you the skills to create your own calligraphic art.\nRegister online or 
 by calling 416-396-3975.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yo
 nge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab543d76074830038293bea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
